runtime: read atomic receipts through bounded safe replacements

Atomic receipt publication can replace a file between lstat and open.
Recheck both safe snapshots for at most three attempts, closing a mismatched
descriptor before retrying and retaining the bounded read on success.
Unsafe files and I/O failures still refuse immediately; lock identity and
lifecycle requests remain unchanged.

Cover actual rename interleavings, descriptor cleanup, readiness without
replaying preparation or spawn, and ordinary stop of retained schema-2 state.
